<section class="fragment-benchmark" data-artifact="benchmark" data-slice="viewer-pitch" data-mode="compare">
  <table class="bm-metrics">
    <thead><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Before (3570eb9 or budget)</th><th>After (36139b4)</th><th>Delta</th><th>Unit</th><th>Direction</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="engine"><td>bench.match_wall_ms</td><td>389</td><td>386</td><td>-0.8%</td><td>ms</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="engine"><td>engine.ticks_per_s</td><td>694087</td><td>699482</td><td>+0.8%</td><td>ticks/s</td><td>higher is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="engine"><td>bench.cpu_ms_per_match</td><td>388</td><td>384.4</td><td>-0.9%</td><td>ms</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="improved" data-side="engine"><td>bench.peak_mem_mb</td><td>5.97</td><td>5.33</td><td>-10.7%</td><td>MB</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="engine"><td>criterion.tick_step_us</td><td>1.4378</td><td>1.4434</td><td>+0.4%</td><td>us</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="engine"><td>criterion.steering_pass_22_ns</td><td>898.22</td><td>873.52</td><td>-2.7%</td><td>ns</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="engine"><td>bench.stream_ticks_per_s</td><td>634859</td><td>640584</td><td>+0.9%</td><td>ticks/s</td><td>higher is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="engine"><td>bench.stream_peak_mem_mb</td><td>7.30</td><td>6.66</td><td>-8.8%</td><td>MB</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="page"><td>viewer.fps_median</td><td>budget 60</td><td>60 at refresh_hz 60</td><td>first value</td><td>fps</td><td>higher is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="regressed" data-side="page"><td>viewer.frame_ms_p95</td><td>budget 16.6</td><td>16.85</td><td>budget miss by construction</td><td>ms</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="page"><td>viewer.decode_us_per_frame</td><td>budget 25</td><td>0.083</td><td>first value</td><td>us</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="page"><td>viewer.page_bytes</td><td>budget 314572800</td><td>31924655</td><td>first value</td><td>bytes</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
      <tr data-tone="neutral" data-side="page"><td>viewer.history_bytes</td><td>budget 25380000</td><td>25380000</td><td>first value</td><td>bytes</td><td>lower is better</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">No tripwire fired</div><div class="callout-body">The eight engine metrics moved less than 1 percent in time and dropped in memory. The slice changed no engine code, so the 10.7 percent peak-memory drop is recorded and not credited to code. The page metrics are first values against their budgets and become the baseline for viewer-match-day.</div></aside>

  <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">viewer.frame_ms_p95: budget-definition defect</div><div class="callout-body">The budget of 16.6 ms is below one 60 Hz frame interval of 16.67 ms. The p95 of animation-frame intervals measures the panel, not the work per frame, so no page can meet it at 60 Hz. The reading is 16.69 to 16.85 ms with a median of 60 fps. Verify recorded it as a Skip; viewer-match-day re-states the budget relative to refresh_hz.</div></aside>

  <style>
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics th, .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics td { text-align: left; padding: 6px 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(127,127,127,0.25); }
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics tr[data-tone="improved"] td:nth-child(4) { color: #1a7f37; font-weight: 600; }
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics tr[data-tone="regressed"] td:nth-child(4) { color: #b35900; font-weight: 600; }
    .fragment-benchmark .bm-metrics tr[data-side="page"] td:first-child { font-style: italic; }
    .fragment-benchmark .callout { margin-top: 12px; }
  </style>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var root = document.currentScript.closest('.fragment-benchmark');
      var metrics = root ? root.querySelectorAll('.bm-metrics tbody tr').length : 0;
      window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('sdlc:fragment-ready', { detail: { name: 'benchmark', artifact: 'benchmark', counts: { metrics: metrics, regressions: 0, improvements: 1 } } }));
    })();
  </script>
</section>
